Venetium 0064 - Windows RT 8.0 / 8.1 support for the ARM32 build (the Chromium side; no extra DLL).
Used by the v1.3 Thumb-2 build together with the V8 Thumb-2 port (github.com/hamed7ir/v8-thumb2-rt): Windows RT 8.x only
runs Thumb-2 code, so the A32 V8 cannot run there, and the browser itself needed these 14 files. Every gap was measured
against the Windows 8.0 RTM system DLLs (6.2.9200) and the browser was run on a Surface RT with Windows RT 8.1.
Windows 10 stays on the old code paths: run-time lookups fall back only where a function is missing, version gates use
base::win::GetVersion(), and the delay-load stand-ins only replace what would otherwise be a crash.
- build/config/win/BUILD.gn: ARM32 PEs say OS/subsystem 6.02 (the 8.x loader refuses EXEs newer than the OS; 10.0 before).
- DiscardVirtualMemory (8.1 Update) was a static import of chrome.dll: looked up at run time (base and PartitionAlloc).
- SetProcessDpiAwareness (shcore, 8.1) at every process start: looked up at run time.
- QueryUnbiasedInterruptTimePrecise (Windows 10) behind LiveTicks: QueryUnbiasedInterruptTime below Windows 10.
- ProcessPrng is CHECKed at start-up: RtlGenRandom (SystemFunction036) when bcryptprimitives lacks it (base, PartitionAlloc).
- ANGLE: D3DCompiler_46.dll is tried when D3DCompiler_47 does not load (the shipped _47 needs 8.1 API sets).
- TrimD3DResources: Trim() only when the device has IDXGIDevice3 (8.1).
- ProcessDynamicCodePolicy (8.1) is set only on 8.1 and later; a failing mitigation-mask query is not a NOTREACHED.
- PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_COMPONENT_FILTER is sent only on Windows 10.
- Delay-load failure hook: stand-ins for the 8.1/10-only delay imports (SetProcessDpiAwareness, GetDpiForMonitor,
  GetScaleFactorForMonitor, QueryUnbiasedInterruptTimePrecise, CompareObjectHandles, d3d12 #101,
  NetGet/FreeAadJoinInformation, RoGetAgileReference, ProcessPrng) instead of the crash.
- GetPackagePathByFullName (not in 8.0's kernel32) is looked up at run time (media, webnn).

